      "fontSize": 24,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "9. Viewport & Virtualization",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "9. Viewport & Virtualization",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "baseline": 19,
      "index": "aR",
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "text_384c5364",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 918,
      "y": 1486,
      "width": 794,
      "height": 692,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#172033",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 1129409718,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785922638434,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "Viewport model\n• camera {x, y, zoom, rotation}\n• world ↔ screen transform matrix\n• visibleWorldBounds expanded by overscan\n\nSpatial index\n• R-tree for arbitrary rectangles\n• Quadtree for spatial partitioning\n• Incremental updates on node changes\n\nVirtualization pipeline\n1. Query visible candidates\n2. Filter hidden/locked/clipped nodes\n3. Choose LOD by zoom and object size\n4. Sort by layer/z-order\n5. Batch render\n6. Keep selected/dragged nodes always resident\n\nFor dashboards / 100k rows\n• Window rows and columns\n• Variable-size measurement cache\n• Stable keys and recycled cells\n• Aggregate data before rendering\n• Canvas chart layer for dense marks\n\nDo not confuse\nDOM list virtualization ≠ scene culling;\nboth reduce work, but at different layers.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Viewport model\n• camera {x, y, zoom, rotation}\n• world ↔ screen transform matrix\n• visibleWorldBounds expanded by overscan\n\nSpatial index\n• R-tree for arbitrary rectangles\n• Quadtree for spatial partitioning\n• Incremental updates on node changes\n\nVirtualization pipeline\n1. Query visible candidates\n2. Filter hidden/locked/clipped nodes\n3. Choose LOD by zoom and object size\n4. Sort by layer/z-order\n5. Batch render\n6. Keep selected/dragged nodes always resident\n\nFor dashboards / 100k rows\n• Window rows and columns\n• Variable-size measurement cache\n• Stable keys and recycled cells\n• Aggregate data before rendering\n• Canvas chart layer for dense marks\n\nDo not confuse\nDOM list virtualization ≠ scene culling;\nboth reduce work, but at different layers.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "baseline": 12,
      "index": "aS",
      "autoResize": true
    },
