      "fontSize": 24,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "10. Interaction & Browser Pipeline",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "10. Interaction & Browser Pipeline",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "baseline": 19,
      "index": "aU",
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "text_77eff2da",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1778,
      "y": 1486,
      "width": 794,
      "height": 692,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#172033",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 1909169258,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785922638434,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "Interaction state machine\nIdle → Hover → Selecting → Dragging → Resizing\n→ Rotating → Panning → TextEditing\n\nPointer strategy\n• One canvas listener: event delegation\n• Pointer capture for drag continuity\n• Hit testing: coarse spatial query then precise geometry\n• Throttle visual updates to requestAnimationFrame\n• Coalesce pointer events\n• Separate transient preview from committed model\n\nBrowser pipeline awareness\nJS → style → layout → paint → composite\n• Canvas/WebGL avoids per-object layout\n• Transform overlays using compositor-friendly properties\n• Read layout, then write layout; never interleave\n• Avoid synchronous measure in pointermove\n• Long tasks moved to workers\n• Track dropped frames and INP\n\nAccessibility\n• Logical object tree and focus proxy\n• Keyboard equivalents for all core operations",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Interaction state machine\nIdle → Hover → Selecting → Dragging → Resizing\n→ Rotating → Panning → TextEditing\n\nPointer strategy\n• One canvas listener: event delegation\n• Pointer capture for drag continuity\n• Hit testing: coarse spatial query then precise geometry\n• Throttle visual updates to requestAnimationFrame\n• Coalesce pointer events\n• Separate transient preview from committed model\n\nBrowser pipeline awareness\nJS → style → layout → paint → composite\n• Canvas/WebGL avoids per-object layout\n• Transform overlays using compositor-friendly properties\n• Read layout, then write layout; never interleave\n• Avoid synchronous measure in pointermove\n• Long tasks moved to workers\n• Track dropped frames and INP\n\nAccessibility\n• Logical object tree and focus proxy\n• Keyboard equivalents for all core operations",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "baseline": 12,
      "index": "aV",
      "autoResize": true
    },
