      "fontSize": 24,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "12. Undo / Redo — FE + BE",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "12. Undo / Redo — FE + BE",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "baseline": 19,
      "index": "aa",
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "text_18785221",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 58,
      "y": 2286,
      "width": 1044,
      "height": 712,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#172033",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 788937898,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785922638434,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "Frontend\n• Command pattern: execute() + invert()\n• Group pointermove samples into one semantic command\n• Store intent-level operations, not every frame\n• Keep per-user undo stack and redo stack\n• Optimistic local inverse for instant response\n• Bound history by count/bytes; checkpoint older history\n• Clear redo stack after new divergent command\n\nCollaborative semantics\n• Undo means “undo my last eligible action,” not global rewind\n• Generate a new inverse operation against current document state\n• Inverse references original opId and expected revisions\n• If target was changed/deleted remotely, produce partial/no-op result\n• Surface “could not fully undo due to collaborator changes”\n\nBackend\n• Validate inverse operation like any other op\n• Append inverse to immutable operation log\n• Never delete historical operations\n• Version restore creates a new head/checkpoint, not time travel\n• Optional transaction/undoGroupId for atomic multi-node changes",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Frontend\n• Command pattern: execute() + invert()\n• Group pointermove samples into one semantic command\n• Store intent-level operations, not every frame\n• Keep per-user undo stack and redo stack\n• Optimistic local inverse for instant response\n• Bound history by count/bytes; checkpoint older history\n• Clear redo stack after new divergent command\n\nCollaborative semantics\n• Undo means “undo my last eligible action,” not global rewind\n• Generate a new inverse operation against current document state\n• Inverse references original opId and expected revisions\n• If target was changed/deleted remotely, produce partial/no-op result\n• Surface “could not fully undo due to collaborator changes”\n\nBackend\n• Validate inverse operation like any other op\n• Append inverse to immutable operation log\n• Never delete historical operations\n• Version restore creates a new head/checkpoint, not time travel\n• Optional transaction/undoGroupId for atomic multi-node changes",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "baseline": 12,
      "index": "ab",
      "autoResize": true
    },
