      "fontSize": 22,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "15. FE Deep-Dive Interview Q&A",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "15. FE Deep-Dive Interview Q&A",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "baseline": 17,
      "index": "aj",
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "text_4476ffac",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 58,
      "y": 3106,
      "width": 1073.594828351249,
      "height": 409.2883509843474,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#172033",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1,
      "version": 189,
      "versionNonce": 337297462,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785923160512,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 12.5934877225953,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "text": "Q: Why not render every object as React + SVG?\nA: 100k DOM/SVG nodes create reconciliation, style, layout, paint and memory pressure. Keep React for chrome and use an imperative scene renderer.\n\nQ: Canvas vs SVG vs WebGL?\nA: SVG wins for small accessible diagrams; Canvas for moderate custom drawing; WebGL for 100k objects, batching and GPU acceleration. Use a hybrid overlay.\n\nQ: How do you maintain 60 FPS?\nA: rAF scheduling, transient transforms, culling, LOD, batching, workers, no sync layout, and frame-budget telemetry.\n\nQ: What exactly is virtualized?\nA: DOM panels use row/column windowing; the canvas uses viewport culling and LOD; assets use priority loading.\n\nQ: How do you perform hit testing?\nA: Spatial-index coarse query, then shape-specific geometry; cache inverse transforms and test topmost candidates first.\n\nQ: How do you avoid hydration cost?\nA: SSR only the shell and metadata. The scene is client-rendered after worker decode; hydrate controls by priority.\n\nQ: How do you find memory leaks?\nA: Heap timelines, detached listeners, growing texture/buffer counts, subscription audits, and automated open/close soak tests.\n\nQ: How do you use event delegation?\nA: One pointer listener on the surface; resolve targets through hit testing. DOM overlays also delegate by data attributes.\n\nQ: How do you prefetch safely?\nA: Intent-based, network-aware, cancellable, and budgeted. Prefetch metadata before large editor chunks.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Q: Why not render every object as React + SVG?\nA: 100k DOM/SVG nodes create reconciliation, style, layout, paint and memory pressure. Keep React for chrome and use an imperative scene renderer.\n\nQ: Canvas vs SVG vs WebGL?\nA: SVG wins for small accessible diagrams; Canvas for moderate custom drawing; WebGL for 100k objects, batching and GPU acceleration. Use a hybrid overlay.\n\nQ: How do you maintain 60 FPS?\nA: rAF scheduling, transient transforms, culling, LOD, batching, workers, no sync layout, and frame-budget telemetry.\n\nQ: What exactly is virtualized?\nA: DOM panels use row/column windowing; the canvas uses viewport culling and LOD; assets use priority loading.\n\nQ: How do you perform hit testing?\nA: Spatial-index coarse query, then shape-specific geometry; cache inverse transforms and test topmost candidates first.\n\nQ: How do you avoid hydration cost?\nA: SSR only the shell and metadata. The scene is client-rendered after worker decode; hydrate controls by priority.\n\nQ: How do you find memory leaks?\nA: Heap timelines, detached listeners, growing texture/buffer counts, subscription audits, and automated open/close soak tests.\n\nQ: How do you use event delegation?\nA: One pointer listener on the surface; resolve targets through hit testing. DOM overlays also delegate by data attributes.\n\nQ: How do you prefetch safely?\nA: Intent-based, network-aware, cancellable, and budgeted. Prefetch metadata before large editor chunks.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "baseline": 12,
      "index": "ak",
      "autoResize": true
    },
